= Review session notes with attributions

Each review session opens by naming the snapshot under review and the codebook edition in force.#footnote[The codebook edition is recorded per session, and a mid-session change of edition ends the session.]

Disagreements between coders are recorded per passage rather than per coder, because a passage is the unit that reviewers can actually discuss.#footnote[Passages are identified by their source row number and their position within the frozen text.]

Claims cite the exact revisions they were written against, and a later correction of the source never rewrites those citations.#footnote[Corrections create new revisions, and the earlier revision stays readable beside the new one.]

Supporting and challenging links are stored as separately attributed records, and a reviewer never converts one role into the other.#footnote[The recording author and the carrying-forward actor remain separate fields even for a single person.]

Repeated quotations stay ambiguous and unresolved quotations stay unresolved, with no ranking and no fallback search anywhere in the review.#footnote[An automatic fallback search was removed in the second edition of the review protocol.]

Every analytical number in the session summary is read from the frozen survey rows, and the presentation format is recorded on its own line.#footnote[The format line is checked during onboarding so that no one mistakes a presentation change for an analytical change.]

At the close of the session the reviewer writes a short summary that names every conflict which remains visible in the trace, and that summary is frozen with the snapshot.#footnote[Frozen summaries are never edited; a later session adds a new summary beside the old one.]
